    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** is our undeniable anchor, boasting a dominant 87.01 efficiency score. His matchup against the vulnerable Holmes is a perfect storm for our strategy; he benefits from a +16% boost due to the favorable SP xERA and a crucial +6% dynamic platoon advantage that weaponizes his elite sprint speed. While **Josh Naylor** (73.37) and **Seiya Suzuki** (67.75) also present high-floor, high-upside profiles against Wesneski and McGreevy respectively, **Corbin Carroll** remains our primary engine for both counting stats and stolen bases. **Henry Bolte** also warrants attention; despite a lower base projection, his position atop the order (+10%) and the extreme park factor (+10%) in his tilt against Gore make him a high-leverage play to set the table for the heart of the lineup.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Jose Caballero** on the bench. While his underlying metrics are strong\u2014boosted significantly by a favorable SP xERA of 4.37 and his proficiency at exploiting slow deliveries for base-stealing opportunities (+2%)\u2014he ultimately failed to make the cut due to his absence from the official starting lineup. We prioritize high-volume plate appearances to maximize our 5x5 Roto efficiency, and without a confirmed spot, he could not displace the marginal reliability of **Travis Bazzana** (42.21). We remain cautious regarding the platoon disadvantage faced by **Travis Bazzana** against the southpaw Peralta, but his SP skill adjustment keeps him just above our bench threshold.\n\nLooking at the remainder of the roster, **Gabriel Moreno** and **Mickey Moniak** both cleared the 65-point mark, largely driven by beneficial platoon splits that counteract their park factors. Conversely, we are monitoring **Austin Riley** closely; while his 61.74 score is solid, his presence in the #8 hole creates a significant drag on his run-production ceiling. We continue to manage the health of our depth chart, with **James Wood** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** remaining sidelined on the IL, leaving us reliant on current starters like **Isaac Paredes** and **Max Muncy** to carry the load against their respective left-handed and right-handed opponents. No major weather concerns are currently flagging the slate, so our focus remains strictly on managing the platoon differentials and stolen base opportunities throughout the evening.",
